WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.334 --> 00:00:21.839
"Tom!" yelled Aunt Polly. There was no answer. "Tom!" she shouted again.

2
00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:25.294
"Where is that boy?" she muttered.

3
00:00:25.295 --> 00:00:29.991
Aunt Polly looked everywhere for her young nephew, but he was nowhere to be found.

4
00:00:29.992 --> 00:00:32.120
He wasn't in his bedroom.

5
00:00:32.121 --> 00:00:36.018
He wasn't in the yard, and he wasn't in the kitchen.

6
00:00:36.019 --> 00:00:41.067
Aunt Polly knew that if she couldn't see Tom, he was probably getting into trouble.

7
00:00:41.068 --> 00:00:44.993
Tom was an orphan, and he loved mischief and adventure.

8
00:00:44.994 --> 00:00:47.501
But sometimes he was too mischievous.

9
00:00:47.502 --> 00:00:52.479
"When I find you, I'll give you a spanking." Aunt Polly shouted.

10
00:00:52.480 --> 00:00:55.363
Then she grabbed the broom.

11
00:00:55.364 --> 00:01:00.335
"Where on earth has that boy gone?" Aunt Polly said to herself.

12
00:01:00.336 --> 00:01:03.319
"T-o-m-m!" she screamed.

13
00:01:03.320 --> 00:01:06.989
Her glasses fell to the tip of her long, narrow nose.

14
00:01:06.990 --> 00:01:11.467
As she pushed the glasses back up, she spied something moving under the bed.

15
00:01:11.468 --> 00:01:15.057
"I've got you now, boy!"

16
00:01:15.058 --> 00:01:19.055
Aunt Polly took the broom handle and quickly pushed it under the bed.

17
00:01:19.056 --> 00:01:23.059
She wasn't surprised when she struck something, but it wasn't Tom.

18
00:01:23.060 --> 00:01:28.234
Instead her cat sprang out from under the bed with an angry howl.

19
00:01:28.235 --> 00:01:34.526
Just then Aunt Polly heard footsteps behind her, and she turned to see Tom sneaking out of the closet.

20
00:01:34.527 --> 00:01:39.495
Aunt Polly grabbed the boy by his shirt and gave him a quick shake and a long look.

21
00:01:39.496 --> 00:01:43.450
His hands were filthy, and he was grinning from ear to ear.

22
00:01:43.451 --> 00:01:48.272
"What were you doing in the closet?" asked Aunt Polly.

23
00:01:48.273 --> 00:01:51.894
"Nothing," said Tom sheepishly.

24
00:01:51.895 --> 00:01:54.481
"Nothing!" shouted Aunt Polly.

25
00:01:54.482 --> 00:01:59.523
"Look at your hands. Look at your mouth. Why are you so filthy?"

26
00:01:59.524 --> 00:02:03.265
"I don't know," said Tom innocently.

27
00:02:03.266 --> 00:02:06.104
"Well, I know," said his aunt.

28
00:02:06.105 --> 00:02:11.278
"It's jam, and I've told you a hundred times to leave that jam alone.

29
00:02:11.279 --> 00:02:15.291
Go back into the closet and get me my stick."

30
00:02:15.292 --> 00:02:18.792
Tom gave Aunt Polly the willow stick reluctantly.

31
00:02:18.793 --> 00:02:22.717
"I'm really in trouble now," thought Tom.

32
00:02:22.718 --> 00:02:29.080
As Aunt Polly raised the stick, Tom shouted, "Look behind you! What's that?"

33
00:02:29.081 --> 00:02:36.705
Aunt Polly turned to look, and in a flash, Tom ran out the door and jumped over the fence.

34
00:02:36.706 --> 00:02:45.012
"Oh, darn that boy!" Aunt Polly sighed, and then she began to laugh.

35
00:02:45.013 --> 00:02:49.894
"When will I learn? He's played that trick on me a thousand times.

36
00:02:49.895 --> 00:02:53.870
People say 'an old fool is the biggest fool,' and they're right.

37
00:02:53.871 --> 00:02:56.977
I should know all his tricks by now."

38
00:02:56.978 --> 00:02:59.592
Aunt Polly worried about Tom.

39
00:02:59.593 --> 00:03:05.259
She wanted him to become a good man, but he got into too much trouble and skipped a lot of school.

40
00:03:05.260 --> 00:03:12.268
"If I find out that boy has skipped school again, I'll have to punish him," she said to herself.

41
00:03:12.269 --> 00:03:15.993
"'Spare the rod and spoil the child,' as the Bible says.

42
00:03:15.994 --> 00:03:20.574
I know the Bible is right because that boy is a very sinful creature.

43
00:03:20.575 --> 00:03:24.358
It's all my fault because I don't like to beat him."

44
00:03:24.359 --> 00:03:31.707
While Aunt Polly was blaming herself for Tom's faults, Tom was preparing to celebrate his mischief.

45
00:03:31.708 --> 00:03:34.882
"I deserve a vacation," thought Tom.

46
00:03:34.883 --> 00:03:41.377
"After all, I made Aunt Polly believe that something was actually behind her for the thousandth time.

47
00:03:41.378 --> 00:03:45.403
And they just don't teach you useful tricks like that at school."

48
00:03:45.404 --> 00:03:50.686
So Tom skipped school, and he had a very good time.

49
00:03:50.687 --> 00:03:54.379
Tom got home just in time to help Jim with his chores.

50
00:03:54.380 --> 00:03:58.287
Jim was the young slave who helped Aunt Polly with the housework.

51
00:03:58.288 --> 00:04:01.722
Tom entertained Jim with the tales of his adventures.

52
00:04:01.723 --> 00:04:06.839
Tom's half brother, Sid, listened too because he had already finished his chores.

53
00:04:06.840 --> 00:04:11.710
Sid was the opposite of Tom in almost every way.

54
00:04:11.711 --> 00:04:17.078
At dinner Aunt Polly wanted to punish Tom for eating the jam and fooling her with his old trick.

55
00:04:17.079 --> 00:04:21.450
So she asked Tom many questions, hoping to catch him in a lie.

56
00:04:21.451 --> 00:04:25.288
"Tom, it was quite warm at school today, wasn't it?"

57
00:04:25.289 --> 00:04:30.564
"Oh yes, ma'am. It was very warm," answered Tom.

58
00:04:30.565 --> 00:04:34.734
"Didn't you want to swim in the river?" asked Aunt Polly.

59
00:04:34.735 --> 00:04:39.590
Tom nervously looked at Aunt Polly's face, but it told him nothing.

60
00:04:39.591 --> 00:04:44.421
He said, "I did want to go swimming, but I had to go to school."

61
00:04:44.422 --> 00:04:46.993
Aunt Polly felt Tom's shirt collar.

62
00:04:46.994 --> 00:04:51.434
It was dry, and for a minute she just stared at Tom.

63
00:04:51.435 --> 00:04:58.431
"The dry collar is a trick I've used a million times, but she's never figured it out," thought Tom.

64
00:04:58.432 --> 00:05:02.218
He tried to hide his smile as he watched his aunt's face carefully.

65
00:05:02.219 --> 00:05:09.228
Was Aunt Polly about to punish him, or had he fooled her once again?
